{
  "annotations": {
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false,
    "readOnlyHint": true
  },
  "description": "Suggest whether a clinician should consider referring a patient for formal adult ADHD screening, with the evidence behind it. Runs the safety gate first: if self-harm signals are found the result is address_safety_gate_first and no screening referral is suggested. Then checks whether the patient is already in ADHD care, reads diagnoses, psychosocial codes, visits and medications, and applies the versioned ADHD ruleset (one high-weight signal with two or more modifiers, or two high-weight signal classes, within 1095 days). Returns one of consider_referral_for_formal_screening, no_recommendation, address_safety_gate_first, already_in_care or insufficient_data; the safety gate; every signal checked with its FHIR resources; each rule and whether it fired; exclusions; notes; and data completeness. Read-only. The ruleset is a starting heuristic from published research, not clinically validated. The result is never a diagnosis; a clinician decides.",
